      "raw_text": "University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Library And Information Science Masters Feb 05, 2026 Accepted on Feb 05 Total comments\nAccepted on Feb 05 Fall 2026 American GPA 3.76\nThe website said we’d hear back tomorrow, but I got an email from the interim dean that I was forwarded for recommendation for admission and that my letter from the graduate school would come in 5-7 business days. The email also says that you can officially accept when that letter comes.\r\n\r\nThe thing I will note, however, is that the email seemed as though it was supposed to be personalized, but wasn’t? So I’m not sure if they actually meant to send it out or if it was a glitch or something…if they did mean to send it and this is real, I’m elated!  Interestingly, the application portal says that my application is still ‘under review,’ so I’m wondering if I should email them and see….or if I should just wait until tomorrow.\r\n\r\nMA GPA is 4.0.\r\n\r\n3a/0w/0r/4p….tentatively.",
